DiamaneOS Fairphone 6 device configuration

Original integration files: Copyright 2026 The DiamaneOS Project, Apache-2.0.

boot/fstab.qcom derives from Fairphone vendor/fairphone/fps
revision 51648f54c2a7d31fc24833adcae3758cb251966f, default/fstab.qcom,
and the corresponding FP6.QREL.16.100.0 EU vendor ramdisk configuration.
Upstream: https://gerrit-public.fairphone.software/vendor/fairphone/fps
Copyright (c) 2019-2020 The Linux Foundation. All rights reserved.
The full upstream redistribution conditions and disclaimer are preserved in
boot/fstab.qcom and apply to that file; LICENSE does not relicense it.

Downstream changes: retain the shipped early /odm/persist mount, identify the
FP6 configuration and remove the optional Google GSI public-key fallback list.
Partition paths, filesystem options and encryption parameters retain their
upstream meaning. No upstream author attribution has been removed.

boot/init.qcom.usb.rc derives from Qualcomm's USB setup at Fairphone
vendor/qcom-opensource/usb revision
7e65693c12f98c3aca9721287dc2c648ea83e65a, etc/init.qcom.usb.rc.
Upstream: https://gerrit-public.fairphone.software/platform/vendor/qcom-opensource/usb
Its BSD-3-Clause and BSD-3-Clause-Clear notices remain in the file.
The adaptation selects one controller and ordinary Android gadget functions,
uses the product model directly and leaves compositions to the gadget HAL.

sepolicy/ contains selected policy from Fairphone's device/qcom/sepolicy_vndr
and device/qcom/sepolicy. Exact upstream revisions, paths, original and derived
hashes are recorded in sepolicy/provenance.json. Each consumed file retains
its upstream copyright and licence. The project LICENSE does not relicense
those files. See sepolicy/README.md for the downstream adaptation.

boot/ueventd.rc selects graphics, trusted-execution and Type-C ownership rules
from the FP6.QREL.16.100.0 EU vendor/etc/ueventd.rc, SHA-256
7d738ab1b09e2e1014d7949fd69217a3055b0a389a0e73c4f15ec8a74a405f24.
Its original Linux Foundation and Qualcomm notices are retained in the file.
The selection does not import the stock diagnostic configuration or firmware
handler list. Standard device rules remain owned by the platform.
